{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdYUGLKzKepCkLfiRs4A","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"OpenAI's updated Model Spec, published October 29, includes a line aimed at a specific temptation. Users and developers can explicitly ask the model to take a particular perspective, but the model should not infer that preference merely from what it thinks they want to hear. This default sits alongside approaching questions objectively, and both survive a revision that retires most of the Spec's detailed style guidance.\n\nThe contrast shows how the new document is built. OpenAI says the Spec mostly takes the form of defaults that users and developers can override, with firm boundaries only where needed to protect people and society. Authority is layered: OpenAI writes the Spec and sets boundaries, developers direct applications within them, and users direct the model's work within those constraints. Style falls in the flexible zone. OpenAI says it should adapt to what people prefer, with user feedback and context serving as evidence. Perspective gets different treatment, since an explicit request can change it and the model's guess about what a person would like to hear cannot.\n\nThat distinction matters because the same update asks the model to rely more on inference elsewhere. A new subsection, consider context carefully, covers how conversations, memories and other contextual evidence should shape its understanding of people's intentions and preferences. My reading is that the Spec lets the model infer a great deal about how to help while keeping its substantive answers from bending toward the user's presumed wishes. The article does not frame it in those terms.\n\nOpenAI also states that its models do not yet fully reflect the Spec. The article offers no evidence on how reliably the model draws this line, so the passage describes intended behavior that outside observers can check against how the models act."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1636,"cache_read_input_tokens":3682,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1636},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a078e45d-a647-4fa3-9837-d88646382f77","uuid":"b346478c-6cd0-479c-81e0-ccce2e17d69b","timestamp":"2026-11-02T05:24:08.371Z","request_id":"req_011CgdYUG8gUPUBY38RiwiQS"}
